// =====================================================================
//  3D HAUNTED HOUSE - "The Last Lantern"   (OpenGL + GLU + GLUT/freeglut)
//  Chapter I   : Blackwood Manor        (gothic mansion, 1 ghost)
//  Chapter II  : The Forgotten Wing     (6 rooms, 5 trials, 2 hunters)
//  Chapter III : The Heart of Blackwood (no map, time limit, blackouts,
//                                        2 hunters + a ghost that only
//                                        moves when you are not looking)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//  CONTROLS
//   W A S D  : move            SPACE (hold) : sprint (uses stamina)
//   Arrows   : look around     F : flashlight      E : interact / door
//   U        : UV scanner      M : minimap         H : help      P : pause
//   N        : mute / unmute   ENTER : start/continue   R : restart   Q/ESC : quit
//
//  BUILD (Linux):   g++ last_lantern.cpp -o lantern -lGL -lGLU -lglut -lm
//  BUILD (MinGW):   g++ last_lantern.cpp -o lantern -lfreeglut -lopengl32 -lglu32 -lwinmm
//  BUILD (MSVC):    link freeglut.lib (winmm is linked automatically)
//
//  WHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE "99 ERRORS" VERSION
//   <windows.h> defines min()/max() as macros, which breaks every
//   std::max / std::min call. Fixed with #define NOMINMAX before the
//   includes. Leftover duplicate lines in the HUD were also removed.
//
//  AUDIO (no sound files, no libraries)
//   Every sound (drone, wind, thunder, heartbeat, whispers, ghost moans,
//   door creaks, chimes, stings) is SYNTHESISED at start-up and played
//   through a small stereo software mixer.
//    - Windows : waveOut (winmm)
//    - Linux   : pipes raw PCM to `aplay` (or `paplay` as fallback)
//    - macOS   : game runs silently (no backend)
// =====================================================================
